The translator exposed an avoidable closure-cell complication: a comprehension captures `substring`, introducing nested frames and cell allocation. I’m switching to the equivalent explicit `for` loop with `append`; the supplied semantics executes that directly, and its invariant can track one accumulator list in the heap.
